so there's more DLC coming down the pipe  for battlefield 4 and I figure you're in  one of three camps number one you  already bought premium and you're gonna  play it so you can get your money's  worth  number two your somewhere on the fence  interested but not sure it's gonna be  worth 15 bucks and number three you're  not listening because you're playing  titanfall well I got some good news for  all you number ones out there the new  naval strike DLC is pretty darn solid  three of the four maps are very  enjoyable the new hovercraft is cool and  the new weapons are a nice little  garnish number two is you might find  something to tempt you here and number  three's well just have fun at your rodeo  let's start with the wave breaker map  the main feature here is the central  island which encloses a submarine base  with two channels running through it and  four big doors that can be opened and  closed to control entry to the compound  PwC's spawn in and outside the base for  speedy ingress and egress and attack  boats can maneuver their way in for some  explosive indoor action and if you've  got a real wild card player on your team  you might even see a little bird trying  to maneuver these narrow corridors in a  map pack not big on indoor spaces this  sub hangar is a standout for the way it  intertwines infantry and vehicle combat  obliteration matches are especially  excellent here as teams try to grab the  bomb from the deadly interior get out  past those fiendish doors and race to  the outlying islands to plant the bomb  naval strike also brings a new mode to  battlefield 4 called carrier assault on  omage - titan mode from battlefield 2142  it places two carriers on the outskirts  of the map and plays out kind of like a  conquest match that combos into a rush  match during the conquest Ematic aliy  bombard the enemy carrier on the lost  islands map that means zipping around in  a suite hovercraft with total disregard  for whether you're on land or sea this  amphibious vehicle doesn't handle like a  dream but it's maneuverable enough to  line up a target from far across a  strait or to wind your way over Hills  and deliver pillowy vehicular homicide  to your foes on this map you can also  move between islands on a quad bike if  you stick to the shallows and the  beaches around the central point are a  solid place to deploy the engineers new  anti-air mines these babies will score  mobility hits on helicopters making the  skies even more unfriendly than they  already were okay back to carrier  assault once you've beaten up the enemy  carrier by conquest aboard and attack  two successive rush crates there are two  ways to get in but only one big room for  you to enter and the rush crate is right  there  beware of enemies bursting through the  one-way doors though you might have some  leeway as they try to navigate the  poorly signposted corridors inside if  your carrier is breached you're in a  tough spot some of your team must return  to the ship to defend it while others  need to keep capturing points to breach  the enemy's carrier this last phase of  carrier salt isn't like rush in which  the defenders can hold out and  eventually win unless the defenders also  assault the enemy ship the capture point  bombardment will eventually destroy even  the staunchest crate defense it feels  like the kind of scenario in which a  commander would really help that or you  know being better at the conquest phase  operation mortar is the third map at all  Rocky Hill topped by an old fortress and  riddled with tunnels close quarters  combat gives you a good opportunity to  try out the new SW 40 a burly new  revolver that packs a nasty punch naval  strike also offers four new class  specific weapons recon gets the SR 3 3 8  a semi-auto sniper rifle that works like  a DMR but benefits from the sizable  scopes of the Recon class the engineer  gets a new PDW the SR 2 which probably  won't get a lot of use on the mid to  long range friendly maps of the DLC but  could be helpful  elsewhere support players have this  double drum fed LMG coming their way for  more Budda Budda Budda Budda Budda Budda  Budda Budda Budda and assault players  get both a new AR 160 and an underbarrel  grenade launcher that can fire three  little bombs before it needs to be  reloaded but arguably the coolest new  gun or at least the weirdest is the big  old tiny cannons on operation mortar no  they don't require a crew of powder  monkeys to fire and no it's not actually  that awesome it's slow and has very  limited range but when you get shot down  by one like you're in some lopsided war  between the medieval Ottomans and the  modern Aztecs in a civilization game  it's hard not to be delighted  the last map is Nansha strike and it  kind of feels like the test ranges Big  Brother there's not a whole lot going on  though the satellite Islands surrounding  it do add a bit of flavor to the  proceedings it just doesn't seem to have  the interesting elements or terrain  diversity that make the others so  appealing terrain diversity isn't a  naval strike strong suit as you might  expect but this oceanic expansion is  shaping up to be a solid addition to the  Premium Package and possibly a good pick  for aspiring shark hunters it'll be  available for premium members in late  March and wait did someone say shark oh  no  [Music]
 

